Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||06-15-2001||12:33 PM||||Great job AusFiero! What program did you use to change the colors? I've always had difficulties changing colors without it looking "PhotoShoppy".||||reg||14
Z||000007||AusFiero||06-15-2001||07:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Great job AusFiero! What program did you use to change the colors? I've always had difficulties changing colors without it looking "PhotoShoppy".</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I use Photoshop 6 Cliff. Some pictures do get that photoshop look as you called it from changing colours yes. I found by using hue and saturation to adjust colours then, and this is the crucial part, adjust the brightness and contrast to bring the colour back to reality. The contrast does most of the work. Also these cars have had the body area cut out before recolouring to keep the background and anything that is not paint it's original colour.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
